intersection_types.vlt:18:12: error: no field `name` on type `T & { tag: string }`
  = note: in generic code, an intersection with a type parameter part has only the members of its object parts; callers see the type parameter's once the type arguments are known (#350)
intersection_types.vlt:25:23: error: missing field `b` in `AB` literal
intersection_types.vlt:26:35: error: no field `c` on type `AB`
  = note: objects have a fixed shape; use a `Map<string, V>` for dynamic keys
intersection_types.vlt:15:18: error: `&` combines object types; `Point` is a class
  = note: Velt classes are nominal: use `Pick<Point, …>` for its fields, or a field-only interface
intersection_types.vlt:5:17: error: no value has type `{ k: string } & { k: f64 }`: field `k` is `string` in one part and `f64` in another
  = note: a value of an intersection has every part's fields at once
intersection_types.vlt:6:14: error: no value has type `{ kind: "a"; x: f64 } & { kind: "b" }`: field `kind` is `"a"` in one part and `"b"` in another
  = note: a value of an intersection has every part's fields at once
intersection_types.vlt:11:16: error: `&` combines object types; `Point` is a class
  = note: Velt classes are nominal: use `Pick<Point, …>` for its fields, or a field-only interface
intersection_types.vlt:12:15: error: `&` combines object types; `string[]` is an array
  = note: an array with extra members is not supported: keep the array in a field (`{ items: T[] } & { … }`)
intersection_types.vlt:13:18: error: intersections of function types (overloads) are not supported
  = note: declare one function type with the parameter types every call needs
intersection_types.vlt:32:28: error: type alias `Tree` refers to itself
  = note: an alias may refer to itself when it is an object type or an intersection of object types written out or named by aliases (`Base & { kids: T[] }`) with no field named twice, or a union that names itself behind an array, an index signature, a `Map` or a function type (`type Json = string | Json[]`); give any other recursive type a nominal member, such as an interface or a class
